---
description: Enforce rid-only identifiers on all client-facing interfaces (API, admin, Postman)
---

# Client-facing rids only

**Goal:** Never expose or accept numeric database `id` values on client-facing surfaces.

## Rules

1. Public models use `HasRid`; route keys are `rid`.
2. API JSON and Inertia props emit `rid`, never numeric `id` (`$hidden` includes `id`).
3. Path params and request bodies reference related records by rid (`productId` in the frontend spec means the product rid string).
4. Guest cart header/cookie `X-Cart-Id` holds the cart rid.
5. Postman examples and variables use rids only.
6. Internal FKs may remain numeric `*_id` in the database.

## What did not work

- Exposing autoincrement ids "just for admin" leaks the same identifiers into Ziggy/Inertia and Postman.
